From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [fuxi runtime] virtually allocate host HAL context on fragmented memory

0025 failed before ordinary data or monitor creation: captured hal_attach+0x3c
kmalloc order:5 failure. The HAL context stores host bookkeeping and virtual
register/ring handles; its read/write shadow pointers are separate coherent
DMA allocations. Use the existing zeroing qdf_mem_valloc/vfree pair only for
the host HAL object, matching both attach-failure and normal-detach frees.
Keep operations allocation, DMA shadow buffers, register windows and hardware
addresses unchanged. Existing minidump uses the active VA backend and normal
removal remains before free. No reclaim or retry settings are modified.
Revalidate ordinary Wi-Fi and monitor-header observation after this repair.

diff --git a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hal/wifi3.0/hal_srng.c b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hal/wifi3.0/hal_srng.c
--- a/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hal/wifi3.0/hal_srng.c
+++ b/qca-wifi-host-cmn/hal/wifi3.0/hal_srng.c
@@ -1089,7 +1089,9 @@
 	struct hal_soc *hal;
 	int i;
 
-	hal = qdf_mem_malloc(sizeof(*hal));
+	/* Host register/ring bookkeeping only. Shadow pointer DMA storage
+	 * below remains separately coherent-allocated. */
+	hal = qdf_mem_valloc(sizeof(*hal));
 
 	if (!hal) {
 		QDF_TRACE(QDF_MODULE_ID_TXRX, QDF_TRACE_LEVEL_ERROR,
@@ -1167,7 +1169,7 @@
 		sizeof(*(hal->shadow_rdptr_mem_vaddr)) * HAL_SRNG_ID_MAX,
 		hal->shadow_rdptr_mem_vaddr, hal->shadow_rdptr_mem_paddr, 0);
 fail1:
-	qdf_mem_free(hal);
+	qdf_mem_vfree(hal);
 fail0:
 	return NULL;
 }
@@ -1222,7 +1224,7 @@
 		hal->shadow_wrptr_mem_vaddr, hal->shadow_wrptr_mem_paddr, 0);
 	qdf_minidump_remove(hal, sizeof(*hal), "hal_soc");
 
-	qdf_mem_free(hal);
+	qdf_mem_vfree(hal);
 
 	return;
 }
